{"id":34089,"slug":"a-confucian-confusion","title":"A Confucian Confusion","year":1994,"country":"Taiwan","duration":129,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/34089-a-confucian-confusion","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/26309a3c2d81c6dfc977517b31c2c106/axg3f2mTmRXHdRKFBkqOvqlFtJWqLs_large.jpg","description":"Edward Yang’s first cinematic foray into comedy may have been a surprising stylistic departure, but in its richly novelistic vision of urban discontent, it is quintessential Yang. This relationship roundelay centers on a coterie of young Taipei professionals whose paths converge at an entertainment company where the boundaries between art and commerce, love and business, have become hopelessly blurred. Evoking the chaos of a city infiltrated by Western chains, logos, and attitudes, A Confucian Confusion is an incisive reflection on the role of traditional values in a materialistic, amoral society.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Edward Yang","slug":"edward-yang"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Chen Shiang-chyi","role":"Qiqi","slug":"chen-shiang-chyi"},{"actor":"Joyce Ni","role":"Molly","slug":"joyce-ni"},{"actor":"Wang Wei-ming","role":"Ming","slug":"wang-wei-ming"},{"actor":"Wang Bosen","role":"Akeem","slug":"wang-bosen"},{"actor":"Richie Li","role":"Feng","slug":"richie-li"},{"actor":"Danny Deng","role":"Larry","slug":"danny-deng"},{"actor":"Wang Ye-ming","role":"Birdy","slug":"wang-ye-ming"},{"actor":"Chen Yi-wen","role":"Liren","slug":"chen-yi-wen"},{"actor":"Hung Hung","role":"The author","slug":"hung-hung"},{"actor":"Chen Li-mei","role":"Molly’s sister","slug":"chen-li-mei"},{"actor":"Elaine Jin","role":"Auntie","slug":"elaine-jin"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Edward Yang","slug":"edward-yang"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Edward Yang","slug":"edward-yang"},{"role":"Executive producer","person":"David Sun","slug":null},{"role":"Producer","person":"Yu Wei-yen","slug":null},{"role":"Production compa